          "title": "15.2 Mock Exams with Full Marking Schemes",
          "image": "https://static.cdnlogo.com/logos/u/49/university-of-cambridge.png",
          "video": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zRyylkUiNsc",
          "content": "**Objective:** To provide students with realistic exam practice. This section should include:\n\n**At Least Two Full Mock Examination Papers:**\n\nMock Exam 1 (IGCSE Style): Structured to mimic a typical Cambridge IGCSE Accounting paper, including a mix of:\n\nMultiple-choice questions.\n\nShort answer/definition questions.\n\nStructured questions on sole traders, partnerships, companies, non-profits, incomplete records, correction of errors, bank reconciliation, control accounts, interpretation (ratios). Emphasis on clarity of presentation.\n\nMock Exam 2 (WAEC Style): Structured to mimic a typical WAEC Financial Accounting paper (Paper 1 - Objectives, Paper 2 - Theory & Practice).\n\nObjective questions (multiple-choice).\n\nTheory questions (definitions, explanations, differences, advantages/disadvantages).\n\nLonger, structured calculation-based questions often involving more complex final accounts of sole traders/partnerships/companies with numerous adjustments, bills of exchange calculations, departmental accounts (if in syllabus), etc.\n\n(Alternatively, a combined mock could be created highlighting question variants).\n\n**Full Marking Schemes and Model Answers:**\n\nFor Multiple-Choice: Correct answer key.\n\nFor Structured/Calculation Questions:\n\nDetailed step-by-step worked solutions.\n\nAllocation of marks (e.g., marks for correct format, correct figures, correct workings, correct principles applied). This helps students understand how marks are awarded.\n\nExaminer's comments or common pitfalls related to each question.\n\n**Example of a Structure for a Mock Question (Simplified):**\n\nMock Exam Question (WAEC Style - Extract from Section B)\n\"The following trial balance was extracted from the books of XYZ Trading Co. (a sole proprietor) as at 31 December 20XX...\" (followed by trial balance and a list of 5-7 adjustments like closing stock, accruals, prepayments, depreciation, provision for doubtful debts).\n\"You are required to prepare:\n(a) The Income Statement for the year ended 31 December 20XX. (15 marks)\n(b) The Statement of Financial Position as at 31 December 20XX. (10 marks)\"\n\n**Marking Scheme Guide for the Mock:**\n\nIncome Statement: Marks for correct sales figure, calculation of COGS, correct gross profit, correct listing and calculation of expenses (with workings for adjustments like depreciation/doubtful debts), correct net profit. Marks for format.\n\nBalance Sheet: Marks for correct NCA values (cost, accumulated depreciation, NBV), current asset values (stock, debtors less provision, prepayments, bank/cash), capital section (opening + profit - drawings), non-current liabilities, current liabilities (creditors, accruals). Marks for format and balance sheet agreeing.\n\n(This section requires creating full new exam papers and detailed solutions, which is a significant task. The focus here is the structure and intent of this part of the textbook.)",
